---
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---

<SiteLayout title="Product Intake System | Ethan Nguyen">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10">
    <header class="space-y-2">
      <a class="text-sm underline decoration-slate-300 hover:decoration-slate-600" href="/">← Back</a>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Product Intake System</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-700">
        Centralized intake + triage to align priorities across teams and reduce ad-hoc work.
      </p>
    </header>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">The Problem</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Requests were arriving via multiple channels with unclear ownership, inconsistent details, and no reliable prioritization.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Context</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700">
        <li>Multiple stakeholders submitting requests</li>
        <li>Limited visibility into status and priority</li>
        <li>Teams losing time to coordination overhead</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Solution</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700">
        <li>Standardized intake form + required fields</li>
        <li>Triage ritual with clear decision owners</li>
        <li>Status taxonomy + dashboards for visibility</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">Results</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5 text-slate-700">
        <li>Reduced duplicate requests and follow-ups (add your metric later)</li>
        <li>Improved stakeholder clarity and response time</li>
        <li>Increased roadmap signal quality</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold">What I Learned</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-slate-700">
        Great systems are lightweight, consistent, and owned—rituals matter as much as tooling.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
